  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Dispatch drives the walk\n\n`run(plan, table)` looks up each string in `table` and calls that function. A new maze is a new plan array — not a new pile of copy-paste moves.\n\nIf a key is missing, a careful runner throws or names the unknown key. A silent skip hides a typo forever.\n\nPlan `\"e\"`, `\"e\"`, `\"s\"` should put the fox on the beacon at (2, 1). A stray `\"n\"` should not vanish."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "missing-key",
      "promptMd": "If `plan` has `\"n\"` and `table` has no `n`, a careful runner should…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "skip",
          "md": "Skip silently forever"
        },
        {
          "id": "throw",
          "md": "Throw or say the unknown key"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "throw"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "missing-plan",
      "kind": "cloze",
      "promptMd": "A missing plan key should {{a}}.",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "throw or name it",
              "md": "throw or name it"
            },
            {
              "id": "skip forever",
              "md": "skip forever"
            },
            {
              "id": "walk east",
              "md": "walk east"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "a": "throw or name it"
      },
      "explainMd": "Unknown commands are faults. Name them or throw so a typo cannot hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "run-plan",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `run(plan, table)` with table keys `e` / `s`. Reach the beacon at (2, 1).",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Walk the plan in order. Each string is a key in `table`."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "If `table[key]` is missing, throw. If it exists, call it."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "for (const key of plan) table[key]()"
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "function run(plan, table) {\n  for (const key of plan) {\n    if (!table[key]) throw new Error(\"unknown \" + key)\n    table[key]()\n  }\n}\nconst table = { e: () => Player.move(\"east\"), s: () => Player.move(\"south\") }\nrun([\"e\", \"e\", \"s\"], table)\nmodule.exports = { run }"
        }
      ],
